    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκπλεος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> neut.
		pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκπλεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					38.20
				</span></i>
			 : poet.<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκπλειος</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> : 
				Att.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκπλεως</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span> :—<i>quite full</i> of a
			thing, c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαιτός, βορᾶς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				247
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				416
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>complete,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖρος τρίγυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
					2.31
				</span></i>
			 ; of a number of soldiers, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππεῖς ἔκπλεῳ..εἰς τοὺς μυρίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.2.7
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>abundant, copious,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτήδεια</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.6.7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
			</span></i> l.c.</div>
